WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.970
Hawkeye started out as a supervillain back
in 1964, but soon switched sides and teamed

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:11.140
up with the Avengers in 1965 — and he’s
been a key player in the Marvel universe ever

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.140
since.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.150
From his cameo appearance in 2011's Thor,
to his expanded roles in the Avengers movies

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:20.650
and Captain America: Civil War, Hawkeye is
a fixture of the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:21.650
these days.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:26.160
The studio was wise enough to lock up-and-comer
Jeremy Renner into a longterm contract early

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.680
on, and he’s become a star in his own right
over the past few years.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.910
So why won't Marvel give Hawkeye a movie?

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:32.910
Fatigue

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.810
Renner has been a cog in the Marvel machine
for a while now, but he was famously unhappy

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.360
with his role in The Avengers.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.340
The actor made it clear he felt his character
was short-changed, and considering he spent

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.969
most of the movie mindlessly brainwashed and
working for Loki, it's hard to argue.

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:48.140
He told Hero Complex:

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.050
“At the end of the day, 90 percent of the
movie, I’m not the character I signed on

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.050
to play.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.931
I’m literally in there for two minutes,
and then all of a sudden…”

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:59.190
Thankfully, he's warmed up to his superhero
role since then.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:04.590
During a Reddit AMA while promoting Avengers:
Age of Ultron, he said he would “be game”

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:07.270
if Marvel ever wanted to make a superhero
movie.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.190
But, he’ll be six movies in after the next
two Avengers films.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.780
He may be game for now, but it's hard not
to wonder how long he’ll be interested in

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.600
playing Marvel’s man who can’t miss.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.380
"I've done the whole mind control thing...not
a fan."

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.480
But let's assume Marvel starts to look at
Hawkeye's comic book history for inspiration.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.830
Well, they may not find much…

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.130
Short on stories

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:31.510
Hawkeye has been around the comic scene for
decades, but he doesn’t really have a lot

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.520
of iconic stories that would translate well
to the big screen.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.000
There’s a reason fans have been begging
for a Black Widow movie — the super spy

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.220
has a mysterious backstory well worth exploring.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.710
The same goes for fellow heroes like The Winter
Soldier, Hulk, and Black Panther.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:49.130
But Age of Ultron already filled in a lot
of the gaps in Hawkeye’s story.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:53.780
When he’s not off being a hero, he lives
a quiet life married to Linda Cardellini and

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.860
playing with his adorable kids.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.210
Hawkeye is just a regular guy in the MCU.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:02.060
While that’s part of his appeal, it’s
hard to make a $100 million dollar blockbuster

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.770
about an average guy.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.270
Speaking of which…

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.520
The Fraction Factor

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:11.700
Writer Matt Fraction’s 2012 Hawkeye series
was one of the most acclaimed comics Marvel

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.060
has published in years.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.950
But that doesn’t mean it’d be a good fit
on the big screen.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:20.120
The comic was a hit because it pretty much
ignored the fact that Hawkeye is a superhero,

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.140
and instead focused on his regular life in
a New York City apartment building.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:29.091
Hawkeye hung around with Kate Bishop, a younger
hero who also goes by the name Hawkeye, and

00:02:29.091 --> 00:02:31.670
faced off with a group of Russian gangsters.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.670
It was almost the Seinfeld of comic books.

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:38.120
"Well after ordering, Mr. Seinfeld and Mr.
Costanza debated on whether or not Iron Man

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.190
wore some sort of undergarment between his
skin and his iron suit."

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:41.690
"Uh huh."

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.200
"And I still say he's naked under there!"

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.510
"Oh that makes a lot of sense."

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.510
"Ah shut up!"

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.621
The series was arguably Hawkeye's best outing
in comic books, so fans might think it'd be

00:02:49.621 --> 00:02:51.350
the right inspiration for a movie.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.430
It even won a ton of awards, and was a crazy
fun story — but it didn’t exactly have

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.900
the makings of a Hollywood blockbuster.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.450
Though, it would make one heck of a good Netflix
TV series.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.450
Just sayin’.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.450
Packed schedule

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.680
You’ll hear this one pretty much anytime
you talk about Marvel movies.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.490
They make a lot of them, and there are plenty
more on the way.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:12.450
The studio has released more than a dozen
films, with around half a dozen more already

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.490
in development.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:18.510
You already have Guardians of the Galaxy Volume
2, Thor: Ragnarok, Black Panther, Captain

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.330
Marvel and the next two Avengers films on
the way.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:22.790
And that’s just naming a few.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:26.959
Put simply, there are lots of options on the
table, and Hawkeye has already been in his

00:03:26.959 --> 00:03:28.530
fair share of movies.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.100
Low-power, high stakes

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.900
No offense to all the archer heroes in the
Marvel and DC universes, but Hawkeye is basically

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.462
a guy fighting aliens and giant robots with
a stick and a string.

00:03:38.462 --> 00:03:39.462
Hawkeye said it himself.

00:03:39.462 --> 00:03:45.730
"Ok look, the city is flying, we're fighting
an army of robots...and I have a bow and arrow.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.280
None of this makes sense."

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.709
But Iron Man does make sense because he has
cool, high-tech armor.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:55.060
Thor makes sense because he flies around the
universe bashing bad guys with a magic hammer.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.060
But shooting arrows?

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.580
It’s cool, sure, but it's not on the same
level.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:00.460
"Keep up old man!"

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.950
"Nobody would know...nobody."

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:10.640
There's a reason DC decided to turn Green
Arrow into a TV series.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.900
It seems that skill set is just better suited
for adventures on the small screen.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:15.900
Team-up

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.460
Clint Barton was the heart and soul of the
Avengers in Age of Ultron, and that’s because

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.450
he just works really well on a team.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:25.570
Most of his best moments in the MCU are when
he’s teamed up with other heroes, and he’s

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.290
a character who works best when he has someone
to play off of.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.990
He’s had a lot of interesting story arcs
in the comics over the years, but most of

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.080
them are tied to larger Avengers stories.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.080
He’s died.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.080
He’s come back to life.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.780
He’s even hung up his bow and arrow to be
a ninja for a while — like you do.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:42.980
But, all of those stories were connected to
the Avengers.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:47.690
Age of Ultron was pretty much Hawkeye at his
best, and that’s because it gave fans just

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:53.330
enough to leave them wanting more, as opposed
to two full hours of pure, unfiltered Hawkeye.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.570
So what about Kate?

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:58.430
Marvel doesn’t seem to be afraid of trying
out new characters, so why not give the other

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.669
arrow-person a shot?

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:04.460
If Marvel really wanted to get creative, it
could bench Barton and introduce that other

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:05.650
Hawkeye: Kate Bishop.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:11.520
Kate was introduced in 2005 in Marvel Comics'
Young Avengers comics series, and took up

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.090
the name Hawkeye in 2006.

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:18.320
Over the past decade, she's become a close
friend to Barton, and is arguably the better

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:19.320
archer.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.980
Nowadays in the comics, she’s kicking around
California to work as a hard-boiled private

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:23.980
eye.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.250
So maybe she should get a movie, right?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.340
But there's a problem.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.270
Outside of comic readers, she isn't a very
well-known character at all.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.320
Considering we're still waiting on Miles Morales
Spider-Man to get his own live-action movie,

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.270
Kate seems like a long shot too.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.500
Thanks for watching!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.930
